<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boniface I, Marquis of Montferrat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1150–1207</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Boniface of Montferrat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boniface I, Marquis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>, was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>, which captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1204. Passed over for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> imperial throne, he founded the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a> and led his knights into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, creating fiefs such as Bodonitsa, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amfissa">Salona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>. He sold his claim to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> in 1207.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat.jpg" alt="Boniface I, Marquis of Montferrat" width="320" height="288" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henri Decaisne · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boniface-of-Montferrat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
